9198,20397,96,2.212,1.739,[[10,1]],[["c0e18bed_5e3b3f8b",20,-2,1,"This got inverted."],["c8022cf6_61ed3298",21,-2,1,"The name `BufferDataPtr` doesn't make much sense since it's not a pointer type at all. Maybe rename to `BufferData` or `BufferDataArray`?"]],0,61],[7110298,20402,96,1.229,1.013,[[20,0.93,0,90],[10,0.07,2,6]],[["57475a89_74aeaf4a",22,-4,1,"This should check that padding <= memory_.size()"],["6e04b382_9afd6fe1",23,-4,0,"The volatile keyword here is crucial to avoid TOCTOU as we are deserializing shmem from the renderer. `gpu/command_buffer` uses this in a bunch of places and it needs to stay every time."],["a17f4aa0_f464cc53",22,-4,1,"```suggestion span<const volatile uint8_t> strikeData = memory_.take_first(size); if (!strike_client->readStrikeData(strikeData.data(), strikeData.size())) { return false; } ```"],["cfb92a33_94654584",22,-4,1,"bytes_read should no longer be needed now"],["ee44da39_fd05a61a",22,-4,1,"Can we have an intermediate variable to make this a bit easier to read?"],["437313bf_491b414f",22,-3,1,"There is no way to do a copy from volatile with some base utility? It might be useful to add if you feel comfortable adding to base (and if OWNERs there are ok with it)."],["9a544187_1c45eb1a",22,-3,0,"[1]"],["b55a9b41_1dd98e43",22,-3,1,"This is always true now, maybe we can remove it and rename `AlignMemory` to `AlignMemoryFor` so it's clear we also check the size. Alternatively, and actually probably better, we should could make…"],["55a5b52c_8929ce38",24,0,1,"data_span.subspan(bytes_for_fonts)"],["e41e95bf_f44c03e8",25,0,0,"As a follow we should add GetSharedMemoryAsSpan() so the UNSAFE_BUFFERS can happen there. If you're planning to do more work here I'm happy to +1 that. If not I will add that function just let me…"],["f923f4d3_f398cf1d",24,0,1,"Let's convert to a span immediately here with something like `base::span<uint8_t> data_span = UNSAFE_BUFFERS(base::span(data, span));` then you can use that span to get a subspan later."]],0,62],[7135562,20408,578,5.609,4.283,[[3,5]],[["075b5f12_797a060e",26,0,1,"```suggestion // Allocates up to size bytes. The actual allocated size will be the span's size(). ```"],["646a783a_7bbe28c8",27,0,1,"```suggestion uint32_t aligned_size = RoundToAlignment(std::max(size, 1u)); ```"]],0,63],[7155471,20427,100,3.027,2.297,[[11,0.942,1,95],[20,0.058,1,5]],[["0989b258_ee9f430e",28,-17,0,"How to prove we only read once, and didn't read ahead or out-of-order?"],["ed799055_e8088fc6",29,-17,0,"do we want the volatile here, or do we want to require is_volatile_v<> later on?"],["61dc9e84_3b1f87cb",29,-15,1,"Document the new method here."],["8438a852_e0a08780",29,-15,1,"I'm guessing we don't want to add `volatile` here because that would almost certainly optimize worse. Is it useful for callers to know they are copying out of a volatile thing though? Should the new…"],["cadf26f6_353c64ed",29,-14,1,"After we rename, we can just drop this note too."]],0,64],[7247266,20433,55,0.82,0.522,[[3,6]],[["8786b7ff_8ab83a28",30,-1,1,"nit: can the TODO be associated with an issue instead of a person? (code is our collective responsibility once it is landed)"]],0,65],[7225876,20435,40,0.82,0.522,[[20,0.622,2,25],[21,0.378,0,15]],[["5da0246f_163897a5",31,-1,1,"```suggestion if (!buffer) { ```"]],0,66],[7222550,20443,87,1.637,1.223,[[2,10]],[],0,67]]}